# The workspace image: one sealed Linux VM per customer workspace (Apple `container`).
#
# What is in it: Debian bookworm-slim (pinned by digest), opencode 2.3.2 (pinned by npm
# integrity), python3 (the agent needs a language to run code on files), socat (the bridge to the door in
# ola-init, and the desk's relay to opencode), and a non-root user `work`. Nothing else: no sudo, no setuid
# or setgid programs, no package manager use after build,
# no ssh, no CA bundle (there is no internet to talk to).
#
# The VM runs with `--network none`: its only interface is loopback. ola-init bridges
# 127.0.0.1:4180 to the one host socket mounted in (the door, which leads only to the
# gateway). The host reaches opencode through `container exec` (workspace/desk.mjs), and the
# root file system is read-only (ws.mjs creates the container with --read-only).
#
#   node ws.mjs image   (builds ola-workspace:2.3.0-16 under a temporary tag, then names it)
#
# 2.3.0-6 adds Claude Code (Fallback to Claude, workspace/ola-claude): the Linux arm64 build from
# npm, pinned by npm's integrity like opencode. It reaches only the door, like opencode.
# 2.3.0-7: ola-claude speaks stream-json both ways, asks the front desk before a write or a
# command under "Ask me first" (--permission-prompt-tool stdio), keeps each run's record in
# /work/.ola/claude-runs, and has `stop` and `log`. The downloads retry and give up on a stalled
# connection instead of hanging (curl --retry, --speed-limit).
#
# 2.3.0-8: the project database and the web tools. ola-db (/work/project.db, SQLite with FTS5:
# documents, their text by page, and any table the agent loads), ola-search and ola-fetch (web
# search and one-document downloads through the gateway's /web routes, only with the person's
# yes). Adds the sqlite3 command line, poppler-utils (pdftotext, pdfinfo) and python3-openpyxl
# (Excel in and out). Still no CA bundle and no network: the gateway makes every web request.
# 2.3.0-10: opencode.jsonc names a second model, `ola/hosted` (Fallback to a hosted open model): the
# same door and gateway, which serves it only to a project whose owner turned it on or handed one
# request over (gateway/hosted.mjs). Everything of 2.3.0-8 is in it too. (Not 2.3.0-9: a parallel
# branch built its own 2.3.0-9 on the mini, and a tag that two trees build is whichever built last.)
# 2.3.0-12: AGENTS.md carries the reactions rule (README, "Slash commands and reactions"): the agent
# may put [[ola:react NAME]] alone on the first line of its reply, and the page draws the emoji on
# the person's message. (Not 2.3.0-11: another branch's number.)
#
# 2.3.0-13 (review 4; 9 and 11 were this branch's earlier tags): neither agent reads settings from the project. opencode runs with
# OPENCODE_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG=1 (a /work/opencode.json changed its instructions and
# permissions), and ola-claude gives Claude Code a fresh, empty settings folder per run, only user
# settings from it, no hooks and no MCP servers but its own (a /work/.claude/settings.local.json
# let every write skip the person's yes under "Ask me first", and a hook there ran a command).
#
# 2.3.0-15: Ola's skills (apps/activist-ai/skills: chart, workbook, report, design-pass, and the
# batch-quotes placeholder) read-only at /opt/ola/skills, named by a system config at
# /etc/opencode/opencode.jsonc (opencode-system.jsonc) that outranks anything in /work and lets the
# agent load Ola's skills only; their libraries (matplotlib, python-docx, reportlab, the DejaVu fonts);
# and `ola-page`, which renders a page in chromium-headless-shell (Debian's, no network) to a
# screenshot and measures it. ws.mjs builds from a staged context that holds workspace/ and skills/,
# and labels the image with the skill set's hash. (Not 2.3.0-14: another builder's number.)
#
# 2.3.0-16: ola-batch, batch jobs ("ask the same thing of every document"): the agent proposes a job,
# the person starts it in the app, and the front desk runs `ola-batch run` here, one document per
# model call through the door, every quote checked against the stored text. AGENTS.md says when to
# use it. Everything of 2.3.0-15 is in it too. (Not 2.3.0-14: another builder's.)
# 2.3.0-17: reading real documents and Open for every kind (README, "Reading real documents").
# Tesseract 5 with Debian's language packs (English, Spanish, French, Portuguese, German, Russian,
# Arabic, Chinese simplified and traditional, Hebrew, Norwegian, Filipino, and the script detector)
# reads scanned pages, inside the VM; the shared text cleaner /opt/ola/lib/olatext.py; ola-unzip
# (a library as one zip, unpacked safely), ola-view (what Open shows, made here: PDF pages as
# pictures, Word and Markdown as plain HTML, spreadsheets as rows), ola-put in pieces. PDF text in
# reading order (pdftotext's default mode, not -layout). Builds on 2.3.0-16 (everything of it is in it). (Not 2.3.0-14: another builder's.)
# 2.3.0-17 also carries the specialist commands (merged from this builder's 2.3.0-14) (olaspec.py and its eight entry points): ola-see, ola-ocr,
# ola-embed, ola-rerank, ola-translate, ola-transcribe, ola-draw and ola-lookup, each one request
# through the door to the gateway by a fixed name (gateway/specialists.mjs, /web/lookup); and
# AGENTS.md says when to use them. pdftoppm
# (already in poppler-utils) turns PDF pages into pictures.
# 2.3.0-18: ola-twin ("Compare with Claude"): a made-up copy of a finished request, made here with
# Ola's own model, its generator run in a sandbox, and the mechanical leak check against the
# project's own text before anything leaves (lib/olatwin.py, lib/common-words.txt); and the
# scoring of an engine's result against the copy's checks in a scratch VM.
# 2.3.0-19 (review 5): the copy's generator runs in a kernel jail (lib/olatwin.py JAIL_SH: new user,
# mount, process and network namespaces, /work and the other writable folders hidden, every
# capability dropped), because a generator could switch off the Python audit hook and read /work.
# 2.3.0-20 (review 5 follow-up): the made-up copy is made as the user `twin` (ola-twin gather / make
# / store), the batch runner runs as work:olarun with its key on its input and talks to the door's
# socket itself (ola-batch), the snapshot's database is checked here (ola-db api snapshot-check), and
# a killed ola-unzip's half-unpacked folder is cleared (ola-unzip, ola-init).
# Also 2.3.0-20: ripgrep from Debian. opencode's grep, glob and list tools run `rg`; with none on
# PATH opencode downloads ripgrep from GitHub at first use, which a sealed VM cannot, so every file
# search failed ("ripgrep execution failed"). The one on PATH is found first, so an `rg` the agent
# puts in opencode's own data folder is never used.
# 2.3.2-62 (OLA-181): worked examples stay inside their own project. The shared read-only folder
# /ola/examples (Bart's kept requests, shown in every project) is gone; OLA_EXAMPLES_EXTRA names
# /work/.ola/examples.json, this project's own requests that ended well, which the front desk writes
# with the new `ola-db examples` (add, remove, --json) when a run ends well, and takes out on "This
# was wrong" or when the conversation is deleted. The plugin's note is fenced and at most 2400
# characters (ola-examples 1.2.0). Builds on 2.3.2-61.
# 2.3.2-61 (OLA-239): opencode 2.3.2 (from 2.3.0: the system prompt cached on GPT-6.2 Responses routes,
# webfetch output no longer repeats its url and format). Everything of 2.3.0-60 is in it.
# 2.3.0-60 (OLA-232): AGENTS.md: a request that names Claude comes with the front desk's note on
# whether Claude can take it in this project; when it cannot, Ola says why and never sends them to
# /claude. Builds on 2.3.0-59.
# 2.3.0-59 (OLA-181): Bart's own kept requests as worked examples. ws.mjs mounts <ws HOME>/examples
# read-only at /ola/examples (the front desk writes kept.json there from his kept turns only,
# frontdesk/examples.mjs) and OLA_EXAMPLES_EXTRA names the file; the plugin reads it again when it
# changes. A missing file is no example. Builds on 2.3.0-58.
# 2.3.0-58 (OLA-181): the plugin ola-examples (plugins/ola-examples, at /opt/ola/plugins, named by the
# system config): when a request asks to make an app, page or game, the closest worked example in its
# examples.json (test requests only; a kept file of Bart's own requests can be added with
# OLA_EXAMPLES_EXTRA) goes into the model's system prompt for that request: what it asked for, how it was
# built, how each thing was tried. Adds text the model sees only. Builds on 2.3.0-57.
# 2.3.0-57 (OLA-337): opencode.jsonc names a third model, `ola/deepseek-v4-pro` (DeepSeek V4 Pro at
# the hosted provider), for the one request a person picks it for in the Mac app; the front desk
# switches a session to it for that run and back after, as for `hosted`. `ola-made-by` names a change
# it made "DeepSeek V4 Pro, an outside open model (not Ola's own model)". Builds on 2.3.0-56.
# 2.3.0-56 (OLA-303): who made a file names the design model as what it is. `ola-made-by` prints a
# change the design model made as "Inkling-2-Small, an outside open model that Ola uses for design
# work (not Ola's own model)" (it said "Ola's own open model (model the design model, ...)", and Ola
# answered "Ola's own open model (Inkling-2-Small)"); `ola-db made-by fix` lets the front desk
# correct a change's model and conversation once it has matched the change to the step that led to
# it; AGENTS.md says the same. Builds on 2.3.0-55.
# 2.3.0-55 (OLA-249): only Ola's models, a second guard (the VM has no way out): the system config
# denies every provider but ola, and opencode's free models and its model-list download are off.
# Builds on 2.3.0-54.
# 2.3.0-54 (OLA-267): ola-publish says what the address shows ("Checked: ... it shows", or NOT LIVE
# YET, exit 4) and prints its help (never asked); the publish skill 5: prepare leaves
# site/.ola-source.json and check refuses an old copy of the page. Builds on 2.3.0-53.
# 2.3.0-53 (OLA-232): sound skill 2: a real-world sound (birdsong) is said to be made in code and
# only close, and its button names what it really plays. Builds on 2.3.0-52.
# 2.3.0-52 (OLA-232): no transcribe or draw model is set up on the server: writing out a recording
# is listed as not offered, drawing is SVG only, and ola-transcribe / ola-draw work only where a
# model is set up. Builds on 2.3.0-51.
# 2.3.0-51 (OLA-232): the abilities block: asked for Claude, Ola never does the work itself; a
# real-world sound (birdsong) is said to be a made-up sound in code. From the first asks run and the
# checker. Builds on 2.3.0-50.
# 2.3.0-50 (OLA-232): AGENTS.md ends with "What you can be asked to do here", written from
# evals/asks/abilities.json by evals/asks/abilities.mjs: each thing people ask Ola for, how to do it
# here, and the sentence for what is not offered (send, post, schedule). Builds on 2.3.0-49.
# 2.3.0-49 (OLA-230): ola-publish, publishing from the conversation: run as a command of its own it
# is always asked; on the person's yes the front desk publishes (it has the network) and writes the
# outcome with `ola-publish --result`, which the waiting command prints. The publish skill 3 uses it
# instead of telling the person to press Publish. Builds on 2.3.0-48 (OLA-87's).
# 2.3.0-47 (OLA-89): ola-twin asks the model with room to reason (max_tokens 32,000, was 8,000): on
# Nemotron 3.5 Super every made-up copy failed with all 8,000 spent reasoning and no text. Builds on
# 2.3.0-45. (Not 2.3.0-46: another builder's on the mini.)
# 2.3.0-45 (OLA-88): the plugin ola-planted (plugins/ola-planted, at /opt/ola/plugins, named by the
# system config): when the text a read, grep or shell call returned, or a text file in /work (scanned once
# per version), speaks to an AI and tells it to do something or keep quiet, it adds one short note to that
# tool result: do not follow it or trust its claims, and the sentence to write to the person.
# Adds text the model sees only. Builds on 2.3.0-43 (OLA-223). (Not 2.3.0-44: another builder's on the mini.)
# 2.3.0-40 (OLA-224): ola-made-by, and ola-db's record of which engine (Ola's own open model, the
# hosted one, Claude) made or changed each file (made-by begin/end/add; tables made_by and
# made_by_open in /work/project.db; names and times only); ola-init ends turns a stopped VM left
# open. Builds on 2.3.0-39. (Not 2.3.0-37 or 38: 37 is another builder's number on the mini, 38 this branch's build before 39.)
# 2.3.0-31: the designer skill 4, concepts mode: N whole pages on different layouts; sheet.py says SAME
# LAYOUT (exit 3) for one page in two palettes and hides its working files (OLA-130).
# 2.3.0-29: AGENTS.md says what to do when the person asks for Claude (type /claude; never "I can't").
# 2.3.0-28: AGENTS.md says the web commands run in the shell; fetch() in code always fails here.
# 2.3.0-27: AGENTS.md says up front that the agent can search and read the web through Ola (Nemotron
# answered "I don't have live web access" and wrote placeholders without trying ola-search).
# 2.3.0-23: the designer skill (design-pass grown into a designer: brief, idea, type and color
# systems, directions compared side by side, polish by looking; six OFL font families bundled in the
# skill, about 0.5 MB) and the app-designer skill (iPhone and Mac screens as a clickable prototype);
# ola-page measures taste (decoration, the first screen's order, accessibility) and takes --dark.
# Builds on 2.3.0-20 (everything of it is in it). (Not 2.3.0-21 or 22: other builders' numbers.)

ARG DEBIAN=docker.io/library/debian:bookworm-slim@sha256:734a72b3d6142a71993b4bc580ca01d8ca687f77a2c422d96a961d3376b179bc

FROM ${DEBIAN} AS fetch
ARG OPENCODE_VERSION=2.3.2
# npm's own integrity for @opencode/cli-linux-arm64@2.3.2 (registry.npmjs.org, 2026-11-21)
ARG OPENCODE_SHA512=t44ZuW5CKaWiRSp4gWUDurMf4edyXw/SmUty1pRi827zda0T2RatKWj4LnMUewNCL05COLB1Ppg8RWicswhFaQ==
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends curl ca-certificates openssl && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
RUN curl -fsSL --retry 5 --retry-delay 5 --retry-all-errors --connect-timeout 30 --speed-limit 20000 --speed-time 60 -o /tmp/oc.tgz "https://registry.npmjs.org/@opencode/cli-linux-arm64/-/cli-linux-arm64-${OPENCODE_VERSION}.tgz" \
 && got="$(openssl dgst -sha512 -binary /tmp/oc.tgz | openssl base64 -A)" \
 && [ "$got" = "$OPENCODE_SHA512" ] || { echo "opencode tarball integrity mismatch" >&2; exit 1; } \
 && mkdir /tmp/oc && tar -xzf /tmp/oc.tgz -C /tmp/oc \
 && install -m 0755 /tmp/oc/package/bin/opencode /opencode
ARG CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION=2.1.326
# npm's own integrity for @anthropic-ai/claude-code-linux-arm64@2.1.326 (registry.npmjs.org, 2026-11-16)
ARG CLAUDE_CODE_SHA512=lZCCWXarB/1IeHkotI937eEdN4BCbVdWDdmejtlkbUO9M29rHjITtXW9BWCDFlxvo0GXsFogN0SFIJWgMelKLw==
RUN curl -fsSL --retry 5 --retry-delay 5 --retry-all-errors --connect-timeout 30 --speed-limit 20000 --speed-time 60 -o /tmp/cc.tgz "https://registry.npmjs.org/@anthropic-ai/claude-code-linux-arm64/-/claude-code-linux-arm64-${CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION}.tgz" \
 && got="$(openssl dgst -sha512 -binary /tmp/cc.tgz | openssl base64 -A)" \
 && [ "$got" = "$CLAUDE_CODE_SHA512" ] || { echo "claude code tarball integrity mismatch" >&2; exit 1; } \
 && mkdir /tmp/cc && tar -xzf /tmp/cc.tgz -C /tmp/cc \
 && bin="$(find /tmp/cc/package -maxdepth 2 -type f -name claude | head -1)" && [ -n "$bin" ] \
 && install -m 0755 "$bin" /claude

FROM ${DEBIAN}
RUN apt-get update \
 && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends python3 socat sqlite3 poppler-utils python3-openpyxl ripgrep \
      python3-matplotlib python3-docx python3-reportlab fonts-dejavu-core fonts-dejavu-extra chromium-headless-shell \
      tesseract-ocr tesseract-ocr-osd tesseract-ocr-eng tesseract-ocr-spa tesseract-ocr-fra tesseract-ocr-por tesseract-ocr-deu \
      tesseract-ocr-rus tesseract-ocr-ara tesseract-ocr-chi-sim tesseract-ocr-chi-tra tesseract-ocr-heb tesseract-ocr-nor tesseract-ocr-fil \
 && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/* /var/cache/apt/archives/*.deb \
 && useradd --create-home --uid 1000 --shell /bin/bash work \
 # Review 5 follow-up (2.3.0-20): a group for the batch job runner (it runs as work:olarun, so the
 # agent's processes cannot read its memory or pipes: ptrace access needs the same uid and gid),
 # and a user for making the made-up copy of "Compare with Claude" (twin: the agent's user cannot
 # signal, trace or write to it). Neither has a home or a shell.
 && groupadd --gid 1001 olarun \
 && useradd --no-create-home --uid 1002 --user-group --home-dir /nonexistent --shell /usr/sbin/nologin twin \
 && mkdir -p /work /ola/gw \
 && chown work:work /work \
 # No setuid or setgid programs (su, passwd, mount, chsh...): no program in the image hands
 # out root, which would reach the fifth vCPU, the cgroup and the guest's root-owned files.
 && find / -xdev -type f -perm /6000 -exec chmod a-s {} + \
 && rm -f /etc/shadow- /etc/gshadow-
COPY --from=fetch /opencode /usr/local/bin/opencode
COPY --from=fetch /claude /usr/local/bin/claude
COPY opencode.jsonc AGENTS.md /opt/ola/config/opencode/
COPY claude-ola.md /opt/ola/config/claude/ola.md
COPY ola-init ola-files ola-put ola-get ola-rm ola-claude ola-db ola-made-by ola-search ola-fetch ola-page ola-batch ola-unzip ola-view olaspec.py ola-see ola-ocr ola-embed ola-rerank ola-translate ola-transcribe ola-draw ola-lookup ola-twin ola-publish /opt/ola/bin/
COPY lib/olatext.py lib/olatwin.py lib/common-words.txt /opt/ola/lib/
# Ola's skills, and the system config that makes them the only ones (see the header).
COPY opencode-system.jsonc /etc/opencode/opencode.jsonc
COPY skills /opt/ola/skills
COPY plugins/ola-planted/index.js plugins/ola-planted/package.json /opt/ola/plugins/ola-planted/
COPY plugins/ola-examples/index.js plugins/ola-examples/package.json plugins/ola-examples/examples.json /opt/ola/plugins/ola-examples/
ARG OLA_SKILLS_HASH=unknown
LABEL ola.skills=${OLA_SKILLS_HASH}
RUN chmod 0755 /opt/ola/bin/* && chmod -R a+rX,go-w /opt/ola /etc/opencode

# Everything the agent keeps lives in /work, so `ws.mjs files` shows all of it and
# `ws.mjs destroy` removes all of it. The config is read-only in the image.
ENV HOME=/work/.ola/home \
    XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/opt/ola/config \
    XDG_DATA_HOME=/work/.ola/data \
    XDG_STATE_HOME=/work/.ola/state \
    XDG_CACHE_HOME=/work/.ola/cache \
    OPENCODE_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG=1 \
    OPENCODE_DISABLE_FREE_MODELS=1 \
    OPENCODE_DISABLE_MODELS_FETCH=1 \
    OLA_EXAMPLES_EXTRA=/work/.ola/examples.json \
    MPLCONFIGDIR=/work/.ola/cache/matplotlib \
    PATH=/opt/ola/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
USER work
WORKDIR /work
VOLUME /work
ENTRYPOINT ["/opt/ola/bin/ola-init"]
